---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "For Photographers & Creators — Grosby Group"
seo_title: "For Photographers & Creators — Grosby Group | Reach Latin America"
seo_description: "Represent your photography in Latin America and the US Hispanic market. Grosby Group syndicates your work to the region's leading publishers. Get in touch today."
permalink: /creators/
lang: en
faq:
  - question: "What types of content does Grosby Group represent?"
    answer: "We represent editorial photography across all categories — celebrity, entertainment, sports, fashion, travel, food, news, and documentary. We also work with video content for broadcast clients. We do not currently represent commercial or advertising photography."
  - question: "How does representation work?"
    answer: "We act as your exclusive licensing agent for Latin America and the US Hispanic market. We pitch your content to our network of 150+ publisher clients, negotiate licenses on your behalf, collect fees, and remit royalties on a regular schedule. You retain full ownership of your images."
  - question: "Do I need to provide exclusive rights to Grosby Group?"
    answer: "Our standard representation is exclusive for Latin America and the US Hispanic market only. You remain free to license your work in other territories through other agents or directly. We never ask for global exclusivity."
  - question: "How are royalties calculated and paid?"
    answer: "Royalties are paid as a percentage of each license fee collected. The exact split depends on your agreement and content type. Payments are made on a quarterly basis by bank transfer. Full reporting is provided with each payment."
  - question: "How long does it take to get represented?"
    answer: "After you get in touch, our team will review your portfolio — typically within 5 business days. If your work is a good fit, we will send a representation agreement for your review. Once signed, we begin pitching your content to our client network immediately."
  - question: "What markets do you cover?"
    answer: "We cover all of Latin America — Mexico, Central America, the Caribbean, and South America — plus the US Hispanic market. We have active licensing relationships with publishers in over 20 countries across the region."
---

